oscopy in superficial bladder cancer: development of an economic model</article-title><source>Urology</source><year>2006</year><volume>68</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.urology.2006.08.128</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Malmstrom PU, Hedelin H (2006) Potential cost savings through the use of fluorescence cystoscopy in superficial bladder cancer: development of an economic model. Urology 68(Suppl 1):40&#x02013;41. doi:10.1016/j.urology.2006.08.128 </citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sylvester</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Oosterlinck</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Meijden</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A single immediate postoperative instillation of chemotherapy decreases the risk of recurrence in patients with stage Ta T1 bladder cancer: a meta-analysis of published results of randomized clinical trials</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2004</year><volume>171</volume><fpage>2186</fpage><lpage>2190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.ju.0000125486.92260.b2</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Sylvester RJ, Oosterlinck W, van der Meijden AP (2004) A single immediate postoperative instillation of chemotherapy decreases the risk of recurrence in patients with stage Ta T1 bladder cancer: a meta-analysis of published results of randomized clinical trials. J Urol 171:2186&#x02013;2190. doi:10.1097/01.ju.0000125486.92260.b2 quiz 2435 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15126782</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR26"><label>26.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tolley</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Parmar</surname><given-names>MK</given-name